#### ⚠️ MEDIUM — Smell 5: Eager Test

**Test:** `OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds` (line 52)
**Research ref:** Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020 — "Eager Test"

```csharp
// ❌ 7 distinct production methods in one test
processor.ValidateOrder(order);
processor.CalculateTotal(order);
processor.ApplyDiscount(order, "SAVE10");
processor.ReserveInventory(order);
processor.ProcessPayment(order, new CreditCard("4111111111111111"));
processor.SendConfirmation(order);
processor.UpdateOrderHistory(order);
```

**Risk:** When this test fails, you don't know which of the 7 calls broke. Diagnosis requires debugging every step.

**Fix — test each step individually, or if this is meant as an integration test, mark it explicitly:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("Integration")]
public void OrderProcessor_FullWorkflow_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
```

Or split into focused unit tests: `ApplyDiscount_ValidCode_ReducesTotal`, `ReserveInventory_AvailableStock_Succeeds`, etc.

