#### ⚠️ MEDIUM — Smell 7: Sensitive Equality

**Test:** `GetOrderSummary_ReturnsFormattedString` (line 122)
**Research ref:** Peruma et al., ESEC/FSE 2020 — "Sensitive Equality"

```csharp
// ❌ Relies on ToString() representation — any formatting change breaks the test
Assert.AreEqual("Order ORD-001: 1 item(s), Total: $99.99", summary.ToString());
```

**Risk:** If the summary object changes its `ToString()` format (e.g. currency symbol, spacing), the test fails even though the data is correct.

**Fix — assert on structured properties:**

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual("ORD-001", summary.OrderId);
Assert.AreEqual(1, summary.ItemCount);
Assert.AreEqual(99.99m, summary.Total);
```

