#### ⚠️ MEDIUM — Smell: Assertion Roulette *(Extended catalog)*

**Test:** `CalculateTotal_ReturnsCorrectAmount` (line 69)
**Research ref:** Peruma et al., CASCON 2019 — "Assertion Roulette"

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(247.50m, order.TotalAmount);  // no message
Assert.AreEqual(22.28m, order.TaxAmount);     // no message
Assert.AreEqual(269.78m, order.GrandTotal);   // no message
```

Three assertions, zero descriptive messages. When one fails, the MSTest runner reports only the expected/actual mismatch with no indication of *which* amount was wrong.

**Fix — add messages:**

```csharp
Assert.AreEqual(expectedSubtotal, order.TotalAmount, "Subtotal mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedTax, order.TaxAmount, "Tax mismatch");
Assert.AreEqual(expectedGrand, order.GrandTotal, "Grand total mismatch");
```

