### 3 · Smell-Free Patterns ✅

`ValidateOrder_NullOrder_ThrowsArgumentNullException` (line 155) is exemplary:

- Uses `Assert.ThrowsException<T>` instead of try/catch
- Asserts on a specific property (`ex.ParamName`)
- Single, focused assertion target
- No external dependencies, no magic numbers, no control flow

This is the model the other tests should follow.

